  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02CG">Exercise <span data-tag="02CG">111.1.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring, and ${\mathfrak m}$ a maximal ideal. In $A[X]$ let $\tilde{\mathfrak m}_1 = ({\mathfrak m}, X)$ and $\tilde{\mathfrak m}_2 = ({\mathfrak m}, X-1)$. Show that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A[X]_{\tilde{\mathfrak m}_1} \cong A[X]_{\tilde{\mathfrak m}_2}.  \]
</div>
